{% comment %}
  Per-order purchase limits: one exact row per product handle/SKU.

  These limits are separate from customer-order-limit-config.liquid. A product
  may have either limit, both limits, or neither. Changing or removing a row here
  never changes the per-customer allowance or its refresh window.

  Each row takes two values:

    order_limit_handle   Exact EasyStore product handle (or SKU where the
                         storefront exposes that identifier), normalized to
                         lowercase at runtime.
    order_limit_maximum  units of that product allowed in one order/cart. 0 or a
                         missing row leaves the product unlimited per order.

  A single row is the whole configuration change. To add another independently
  managed order limit, add another row; no numbered slot, JavaScript list, or
  second file needs to be updated:

    {% raw %}{% include 'per-order-limit-row', order_limit_handle: 'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN', order_limit_maximum: 2 %}{% endraw %}
    {% raw %}{% include 'per-order-limit-row', order_limit_handle: 'MTG-HOB-DNK-EN', order_limit_maximum: 4 %}{% endraw %}

  This scales to large handle matrices because the rows publish configuration
  only. The cart is scanned once by per-order-limits.liquid and shared across all
  rows rather than scanned again for every configured product.

  The examples above are documentation only. Keep active business values below
  this comment; customer-wide limits remain in customer-order-limit-config.liquid.
{% endcomment %}

{% include 'per-order-limit-row', order_limit_handle: 'MTG-FRA-CBB-EN', order_limit_maximum: 1 %}
